    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      84.67,
      634.84,
      522.27,
      650.68
    ],
    "text": "Fernando vs. Curera (1 N.L.R. 29) where Bonser CJ held that it was the duty of the court",
    "fonts": [
      "Helvetica",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.619373321533203,
      11.800000190734863,
      12.422006607055664
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      84.68,
      655.25,
      522.27,
      671.0
    ],
    "text": "to fix a day for hearing. In Lorensu Apuhamy vs. Paaris (11 N.L.R. 202) Wood Renton J",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.589014053344727,
      11.800000190734863
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      85.3,
      675.89,
      522.67,
      691.64
    ],
    "text": "(With whom Hutchinson C.J. agreed) held that the duty affixing the day of trial is vested",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.800000190734863,
      12.28911304473877
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      85.34,
      695.81,
      522.83,
      711.56
    ],
    "text": "on the court. The judgment of Wood Renton J was followed by Lascelles C.J. in Kuda",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.800000190734863,
      12.28911304473877
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      514.25,
      743.99,
      612.17,
      769.52
    ],
    "text": "2 t f",
    "fonts": [
